CORE
main.c
--unwind 4 --rounds 3 --por --allow-pointer-unsoundness --no-assertions --datarace
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
--
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
--
The new thread publishes the address of its own copy of `slot`, and main
writes through it while the thread writes `slot`: a real race on the
thread's copy. Recording the copy's initialisation in the new thread must
not hide it. FAILED before and after the fix.
